      "props": {
        "lastUpdated": "2026-05-07",
        "title": "About the Temple",
        "content": [
          "MyPoojaBooking is an authorised digital platform for booking poojas and sevas at Shree Dwarkadhish Temple, Dwarka. We provide authentic spiritual services and direct temple booking facility for devotees worldwide.",
          "Shree Dwarkadhish Temple, also known as the Jagat Mandir, is a Hindu temple dedicated to Lord Krishna, who is worshipped here by the name Dwarkadhish, or 'King of Dwarka'. The temple is located at Dwarka city, Gujarat, India, which is one of the destinations of Char Dham, a Hindu pilgrimage circuit.",
          "The main shrine of the five-storied building, supported by 72 pillars, is known as Jagat Mandir or Nija Mandir. Archaeological findings suggest it is 2,200 - 2,500 years old. The temple was enlarged in the 15th-16th century. According to tradition, the original temple was believed to have been built by Krishna's grandson, Vajranabha, over the hari-griha (Lord Krishna's residential place)."
        ],
        "image": "/assets/images/dwaraka_temple/dwaraka.png",
        "badgeText": "The temple dates back to almost 2,500 years, making it one of the oldest spiritual destinations.",
        "ctas": [
          {
            "text": "Book Pooja",
            "link": "/book/dwarkadhish",
            "variant": "primary"
